In <5sOC947_tBB@rsl000.rhein-main.de>, rschuhl@rsl000.rhein-main.de (Robert Schuhl) writes:
>
>I try to print over /dev/lp0 to a printer (HP XL 300), but the device says  
>alway 'device offline'? (also in lpc) What did I wrong? I installed it  
>like a usual serial printer, just changed the device. The cable seems o.k.
>Who can help?
>Robert

The problem might be in the fact that you set it up like a serial printer.  In the
printcap there is a parameter "rw" which opens the printer device for reading and
writing.  If you have it on the parallel port, the printer and port may not support
both reading and writing but the printer driver expects it to.  Remove the rw
from your /etc/printcap file for this printer and see if that helps.  It worked for me.

