> Does anybody of you have any information about the OSF-DME
> (Distributed Management Environment).
> How does it work ?  What Standards are involved ?
> How is it structured ? .....

> I am about to write a report about it and all I've got
> are some articles from some magazines with really THIN infos.


Unofficial Information Follows 8-) 8-) 8-)

Your report is likely to be pretty thin, unless it is meant to be
historical.  The OSF-DME project was cancelled some time ago.

The original intent was to gather together a lot of technologies and
then to glue them together into one shared GUI and one shared underlying
distributed object engine.  For various technical, commercial, personal,
and political reasons, OSF eventually gave up.

HOWEVER

most of the technology is still around, and still fits together in
various more or less simple ways.  Since I work for HP, I am familiar
with the HP OpenView framework, HP Software Distributor, HP NetLS
software license manager, etc etc etc.  

Likewise, Tivoli's system admin products were part of DCE (I think).
Surely other vendors were supplying various parts.

CONCLUSION

DME is still around, just not as a single unified technology from OSF.
Instead, DME is a loose federation of vendors who build system and
network management tools that interoperate to some degree.




